  "autoBackupIntro": "While your vault is open, KeyKey writes an encrypted backup to the folder you choose whenever an entry changes. It is the same as a backup you make yourself: it opens with the master password or recovery key you had when it was made. The newest 5 backups and the last backup of each of the newest 14 days are kept; older ones are deleted. Backups you make yourself are never touched.\n\nSo that your backups don't disappear with your phone, choose a folder that a sync app such as Syncthing or Nextcloud copies elsewhere. Google Drive may not appear in the folder list. The sync app moves the backup; KeyKey never sends it anywhere.\n\nEvery backup in the folder is another copy on which someone who gets the file could try to guess your master password; use a strong one.",
